/*Q16. Write a Java program to define a class Student with the following data members:
• name - to store the name of the student (String)
• age - to store the age of the student (Integer)
The class should contain the following member functions:
• input() - Reads the student's name and age from standard input and stores them in the corresponding instance variables.
• display() - Displays the student's name and age on separate lines in the required format.
The StudentDetails class should create a Student object, call input() to read the student details, and then call display() to display them.
Input Format:
• The first line contains the student's name (String).
• The second line contains the student's age (int).
Output Format:
• Display the student name and age in the following format:
Name: <student_name>
Age: <student_age>
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
class Student {
    String name;
    int age;
 
    void input(Scanner sc) {
        name = sc.nextLine().trim();
        age = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
    }
 
    void display() {
        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
    }
}
 
public class StudentDetails {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        Student s = new Student();
        s.input(sc);
        s.display();
        sc.close();
    }
}
